WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.830
Alien: Covenant promised to explore the mysterious
and goopy lineage of the xenomorph species

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:07.420
that we all know and love.

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:13.429
But in many cases, it just left the entire
Alien franchise open to even more questions.

00:00:13.429 --> 00:00:18.550
Let's burrow into Covenant, stick our ovipositors
down its throat, and see how many answers

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:19.960
are still waiting to hatch.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.820
And, of course, spoilers are hatching beyond
this point.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.220
So cover your face, okay?

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:26.340
Who are the Engineers?

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:31.450
More than anything else, Covenant needed to
explain just what the heck its prequel Prometheus

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:32.450
was all about.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:37.600
Prometheus introduced us to the Engineers,
an alien race who inexplicably started life

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:38.600
on Earth.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.710
We don't know exactly why, and that's what
the crew of the Prometheus sets out to discover.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:46.880
"What we hope to achieve, was to meet our
makers—to get answers.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.839
Why they even made us in the first place."

00:00:49.839 --> 00:00:54.999
However, once the android David actually finds
the Engineers and all of the answers are within

00:00:54.999 --> 00:00:56.850
reach… he slimes them.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:01.609
An entire city of Engineers is destroyed by
David's stock of evil black goo.

00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:06.710
We never learn who the Engineers are, why
they do what they do, or where they came from.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.430
And thanks to David, we may never know.

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:11.640
Why did David kill the Engineers?

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:16.540
The motivations of the Covenant's human crew
are pretty straightforward: just don't die.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:21.160
However, the Alien franchise's androids tend
to be a little harder to read, and none are

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:22.350
more confusing than David.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:27.710
It becomes clear in both Prometheus and the
introduction to Covenant that David sees himself

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:33.020
as superior to humans, and even expresses
the bizarre idea that all creations want to

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:34.280
kill their creators.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:38.700
"Kill all humans, must kill all humans."

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:43.020
Sure, you might be mad at mom for not letting
you borrow the car on a school night, but

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.780
that's pretty much the extent of matricidal
rage that most people reach.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:49.930
So why exactly does David wipe out the Engineers?

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:55.480
It's possible that, as mankind's implied creators,
David is just taking his murder plot one step

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:59.700
deeper into his ancestry, but there isn't
a whole lot of meaning there.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:03.530
And he definitely doesn't do it to protect
Earth from the Engineers.

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:05.090
So what's the deal?

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:06.670
What did the goo do?

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:11.790
When we meet David again in Covenant, he leads
the crew into the derelict city of the Engineers,

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.870
through masses of their dead bodies.

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:16.390
Of course, they're all dead thanks to David's
goo.

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:18.640
But what exactly did this goo do?

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:23.370
As far as anyone can tell, it mutates any
living animal it comes into contact with,

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:26.260
but we never find out what it did to the Engineers.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:31.920
If the goo did what goo usually does, the
entire Engineer planet would be swarming with

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:32.920
xenomorphs.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.120
So where did all of those potential xenomorphs
end up after ten years?

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.180
What happened in the five minutes after the
goo drop?

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.590
Why was the Engineers' planet lifeless?

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:46.290
The planet that the Covenant lands on is ideal
for life, but inexplicably, the crew can't

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:47.569
seem to find any.

00:02:47.569 --> 00:02:50.850
No birds, no bugs, just silence.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:56.120
As David tells his guests, the virus he dispersed
was made to seek out hosts, so all of the

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:00.740
meat on the planet became an immediate target
as soon as he dropped his payload.

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:04.890
But none of the 'morphs that would have resulted
from his attack seem to still be around.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:05.930
Nothing is.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:10.640
Ultimately, trying to comprehend what goo
can and cannot do is a job best left for Ridley

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:12.630
Scott's pulsating nightmares.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:17.310
But that mysterious decade where David was
left to his own messed-up devices leaves too

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:19.400
many mysteries for the continuity-concerned.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.970
For now, let's just say it was Predators.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.650
What's up with those spores?

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:29.230
The crew of the Covenant gets their first
taste of alien madness when a couple of dinguses

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:34.540
brush against some plants, suck in some alien
dust, and after a little while, have monsters

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.390
bursting out of their giblets.

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:37.550
It's basic science.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:42.340
Except human DNA and Engineer DNA are, allegedly,
nearly identical.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:47.290
It wouldn't make much biological sense if
the Engineers' planet was rife with a virulent

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.060
strain of murder-monster mushrooms.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:53.379
So these balls of alien death-confetti must
not have always been there.

00:03:53.379 --> 00:03:56.680
Instead, they must have been caused by David's
use of the goo.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:01.180
The goo can mutate every animal it comes in
contact with — so why did it very selectively

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:04.599
choose one plant to turn into a vehicle for
the species?

00:04:04.599 --> 00:04:09.930
Arguably, it's not a plant at all that shoots
out those spores, but that still leaves questions.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:13.510
Were these pods part of David's later experiments?

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:18.550
And if so, why are Facehuggers treated as
a superior form of alien evolution?

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:23.230
The spores' method of propagating the species
is only a million times more efficient than

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:24.710
the alien egg pods.

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:29.740
The choice is simple: your species propagates
because an idiot actively agitates a giant,

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:34.610
ugly egg and waits for its terrifying contents
to attack and shove an egg tube down their

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:39.240
throat...or your species lives on because
something gently brushes against a small pod

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:40.370
with their toe.

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:42.460
The more efficient method is clear.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:46.100
So what makes the eggs more evolutionarily
sound than the spores?

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.460
Is David the xenomorph whisperer?

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:52.510
It's easy to argue that aliens aren't overly
interested in androids because they don't

00:04:52.510 --> 00:04:55.000
really have a lot of delicious edible parts.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:59.050
So if you're a synthetic being, you pretty
much get a xenomorph hall pass.

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:03.140
But why are the xenomorphs David is cultivating
strangely loyal to him?

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:07.330
At the very least, they seem to see him as
one of the only living things that's not worth

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:11.490
immediately killing — which is really saying
something when you're an animal designed only

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:12.490
for killing.

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:16.780
We know xenomorphs don't imprint on the first
thing they see like many Earth animals, so

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:20.620
how does David automatically have this dominion
over the beasts?

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.800
Maybe we'll learn the answer in a sequel.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.240
And while we're on the subject of synthetics...

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:27.470
Is Walter still alive?

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:31.990
Alien is a franchise that relishes showing
the audience every gory detail of nearly every

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:33.030
bloody death.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:36.980
So when someone dies and you don't at least
see their viscera-strewn corpse, you know

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.240
something might be up.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:42.920
During the first phase of the big fight between
David and Walter, we see that Walter has the

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:44.680
ability to heal himself.

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:48.720
While he takes a few minutes to reboot, it
seems like he can recover from some pretty

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:49.720
deep cuts.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:54.860
"Now stand aside, worthy adversary!"

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:55.620
"'tis but a scratch!"

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:57.000
"A scratch?

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:57.980
Your arm's off!"

00:05:57.980 --> 00:05:58.699
"No, it isn't."

00:05:58.699 --> 00:06:03.030
After the second phase of their big battle,
we learn that David comes out on top and switches

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:04.520
places with Walter.

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:06.190
We never learn Walter's fate.

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:10.800
But when even an earlier android model like
David can survive decapitation, we can assume

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.430
that Walter is still alive.

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:14.840
Or can we?

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:17.410
Everyone knows that you can't keep a good
'droid down.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:18.940
Thanks for watching!

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:21.860
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.400
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

